      "id": "I01",
      "fact": "observe() dispatches through one ContextVar, wraps record() in except Exception, then calls invalidate(); session finally calls close().",
      "implication": "Independent adapter may use duck typing through unchanged public session, but record/invalidate/close must isolate their own ordinary faults; existing close timing is not sufficient to assert business completion."
    },
    {
      "id": "I02",
      "fact": "Legacy serialization uses insertion order and ensure_ascii=True,allow_nan=False,separators comma/colon. Codec dump() sorts keys.",
      "implication": "Do not use codec.dump() for logical event JSON; preserve legacy serializer layout and byte encoding."
    },
    {
      "id": "I03",
      "fact": "Legacy ndarray encoder already copies; Codec.add_array() also detaches.",
      "implication": "Delegate the raw array directly to public add_array(); do not copy twice or use private codec methods."
    },
    {
      "id": "I04",
      "fact": "qualification.begin encodes case.case_id; qualification.complete has failures/witness but no operation_id. Codec supports this legacy shape via active operation.",
      "implication": "expected_operations must be the two complete frozen case IDs in order, not literal U1/U2; never add operation_id to logical events."
    },
    {
      "id": "I05",
      "fact": "Legacy comparator _load() builds full events/array lists and expects semantic.jsonl/npy.",
      "implication": "It cannot validate v2 directories; a separate bounded-memory envelope/mode validator and codec streaming compare are required."
    },
